### Expenso API quick tests (VS Code "REST Client" extension or Visual Studio)
### 1) Run the Login request, 2) copy accessToken into @token below, 3) run the others.

@api = http://localhost:5180
@token = paste-access-token-here

### Login as an employee
POST {{api}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "employee1@expenso.local", "password": "Expenso@123" }

### Login as the manager
POST {{api}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "manager@expenso.local", "password": "Expenso@123" }

### Who am I?
GET {{api}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Categories
GET {{api}}/api/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a draft expense (employee token)
POST {{api}}/api/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Client visit - Pune flights",
  "categoryId": 1,
  "expenseDate": "2026-11-05",
  "amount": 2450.00,
  "merchantName": "IndiGo",
  "description": "Return flight",
  "paymentMethod": "PersonalCard"
}

### Validation error example: future date + zero amount -> 400
POST {{api}}/api/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Bad", "categoryId": 1, "expenseDate": "2099-01-01", "amount": 0, "paymentMethod": "Cash" }

### My expenses
GET {{api}}/api/expenses/my?page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Manager: pending queue (manager token)
GET {{api}}/api/manager/pending
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Manager: reject without a reason -> 400
POST {{api}}/api/manager/1/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "" }
